   "q_en": "<p>There is a cuboid with surface area of adjacent faces being A cm<sup>2</sup>, B cm<sup>2</sup> and C cm<sup>2</sup>. Find volume of the cuboid (in cm<sup>3</sup>).</p>",
   "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2360;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; A &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>, B &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup> &#2324;&#2352; C &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup> &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;)&#2404;</p>",
   "options_en": [
    "&radic;(A<sup>2</sup> + B<sup>2</sup> + C<sup>2</sup>)*(A + B + C)",
    "&radic;(ABC)",
    "&radic;(AB<sup>2</sup> + BC<sup>2</sup> + CA<sup>2</sup>)",
    "&radic;AB + &radic;BC + &radic;CA"
   ],
   "options_hi": [
    "&radic;(A<sup>2</sup> + B<sup>2</sup> + C<sup>2</sup>)*(A + B + C)",
    "&radic;(ABC)",
    "&radic;(AB<sup>2</sup> + BC<sup>2</sup> + CA<sup>2</sup>)",
    "&radic;AB + &radic;BC + &radic;CA"
   ],
   "answer": 1,
   "solution_en": "<p>Let l, b and h be dimensions of cuboid.</p><p>Surface area of three faces of cuboid;</p><p>l*b = A ..(1)</p><p>b*h = B ..(2)</p><p>h*l = C ..(3)</p><p>Multiplying (1), (2) and (3); we get</p><p>(l*b*h)<sup>2</sup> = A*B*C</p><p>Volume of cuboid = l*b*h = &radic;(ABC)</p>",
   "solution_hi": "<p>Let l, b and h be dimensions of cuboid.</p><p>Surface area of three faces of cuboid;</p><p>l*b = A ..(1)</p><p>b*h = B ..(2)</p><p>h*l = C ..(3)</p><p>Multiplying (1), (2) and (3); we get</p><p>(l*b*h)<sup>2</sup> = A*B*C</p><p>Volume of cuboid = l*b*h = &radic;(ABC)</p>",
   "marks": 1.0,
   "neg": 0.25
