   "q_en": "<p>Find the total number of smaller cubes obtained if half of a cube which has a side of 18 cm is cut into smaller cubes of 1 cm each and the other half of that cube is cut into smaller cubes of 3 cm each?</p>",
   "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; 18 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; 1 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2328;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366;&#2335;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360; &#2328;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2375; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2325;&#2379; 3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2328;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366;&#2335;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2328;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>",
   "options_en": [
    "2300",
    "4890",
    "3024",
    "1250"
   ],
   "options_hi": [
    "2300",
    "4890",
    "3024",
    "1250"
   ],
   "answer": 2,
   "solution_en": "<p>The side of the cube is 18 cm and the sides of the smaller cubes are either 1 cm or 3 cm.</p><p>Volume of original cube = 18 * 18 * 18 = 5832.</p><p>Half of the cube will be a rectangular cuboid.</p><p>Hence, volume of one rectangular cuboid = 9 * 18 * 18 = 2916</p><p>Volume of smaller cube having length of 1 cm = 1 * 1 * 1 = 1.</p><p>The number of cubes having length of 1 cm = 2916/1 = 2916.</p><p>Volume of smaller cube having length of 3 cm = 3 * 3 * 3 = 27.</p><p>The number of cubes having length of 3 cm = 2916/27 = 108.</p><p>The total number of smaller cubes = 2916 + 108 = 3024.</p>",
   "solution_hi": "<p>The side of the cube is 18 cm and the sides of the smaller cubes are either 1 cm or 3 cm.</p><p>Volume of original cube = 18 * 18 * 18 = 5832.</p><p>Half of the cube will be a rectangular cuboid.</p><p>Hence, volume of one rectangular cuboid = 9 * 18 * 18 = 2916</p><p>Volume of smaller cube having length of 1 cm = 1 * 1 * 1 = 1.</p><p>The number of cubes having length of 1 cm = 2916/1 = 2916.</p><p>Volume of smaller cube having length of 3 cm = 3 * 3 * 3 = 27.</p><p>The number of cubes having length of 3 cm = 2916/27 = 108.</p><p>The total number of smaller cubes = 2916 + 108 = 3024.</p>",
   "marks": 1.0,
   "neg": 0.25
  },
